      "writtenOn": "2023-08-15T13:36:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if we just call this fSampleCount and we just always set it to be the sample count of the whole render pass. We can assert if any attachment has samples the count matches the value here. If this is \u003e 1 and attachments have sample of 1, then we can assert implicit msaa resolves.\n\nNow the checks on whether to do implicit would need to check that attachment having 1 and this being \u003e 1. Or maybe those checks could just look at the cap for implicit feature support. Are there cases where we would have the feature but not use it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "cd7fde035d64e5557402f09b38c468f8fbb95866",
